  Whitespace contract:
    - Fragment body is column-1 Markdown (NO leading indent) — it slots
      directly into the caller's already-YAML-stripped body text, which
      is also column-1 after the `content: |` base indent is removed.
    - Fragment emits NO leading and NO trailing newline. The caller uses
      plain `{{ template ... }}` (no trim markers), so the newlines that
      naturally surround the template action in the caller's YAML block
      become the fragment's leading and trailing newlines.
    - The caller's next line (typically a blockquote continuation `>`)
      follows directly after the template action's line so the blockquote
      stays contiguous — a blank line inside a blockquote splits it into
      two blockquotes in Markdown.

  Recommended caller pattern:

      ## CRITICAL: User Interaction Rules

      {{ template "_shared/no-text-ui" . }}
      >
      > ⚠️ (prompt-specific posting-policy continuation here)

  If the caller has no continuation, the blank line before the next
  heading closes the blockquote normally.
